ProductWiseQueryBuilder — All Cases 

Core Idea 

Every method you call adds a clause to the SQL. Every method you don't call → that clause simply doesn't exist. No empty fragments, no nulls. 

 

The 5 Building Blocks 

 

Case 1: Nothing — just total balance 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder().build(); 

SELECT 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 

No WHERE, no GROUP BY. Just the grand total. 

 

Case 2: Groups only (no date filter) 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder() 
   .groups(List.of( 
       new HeadCodeGroup("CASA", List.of("01036")), 
       new HeadCodeGroup("Demand Deposit", List.of("01042","01043")) 
   )) 
   .build(); 

SELECT 
   CASE 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01036']) THEN 'CASA' 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) THEN 'Demand Deposit' 
   END AS "GROUP_NAME", 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 
WHERE ( 
   ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01036']) 
   OR ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) 
) 
GROUP BY 1 
ORDER BY 1 

What appeared: CASE, ARRAY_OVERLAP WHERE, GROUP BY 1 
What didn't: no date filter, no extra columns 

 

Case 3: Groups + single date (your old query) 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder() 
   .groups(groups) 
   .dates(List.of("21-09-2026")) 
   .searchKey("HEAD_CODE") 
   .build(); 

SELECT 
   CASE 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("HEAD_CODE", ARRAY['01036']) THEN 'CASA' 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("HEAD_CODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) THEN 'Demand Deposit' 
   END AS "GROUP_NAME", 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 
WHERE "DATE" = '21-09-2026' 
 AND ( 
   ARRAY_OVERLAP("HEAD_CODE", ARRAY['01036']) 
   OR ARRAY_OVERLAP("HEAD_CODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) 
 ) 
GROUP BY 1 
ORDER BY 1 

What appeared: date filter with =, CASE, ARRAY_OVERLAP, GROUP BY 1 
What didn't: no groupBy columns, no extra conditions 

 

Case 4: Groups + multi-date + groupBy DATE (your new query) 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder() 
   .groups(groups) 
   .dates(List.of("12-04-2026", "13-04-2026", "14-04-2026")) 
   .searchKey("YSA_HEADCODE") 
   .groupBy("DATE") 
   .build(); 

SELECT 
   "DATE", 
   CASE 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01036']) THEN 'CASA' 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) THEN 'Demand Deposit' 
   END AS "GROUP_NAME", 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 
WHERE "DATE" IN ('12-04-2026','13-04-2026','14-04-2026') 
 AND ( 
   ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01036']) 
   OR ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) 
 ) 
GROUP BY 1, 2 
ORDER BY 1, 2 

What appeared: "DATE" in SELECT, date filter with IN, GROUP BY 1, 2 
What didn't: no extra conditions 

 

Case 5: Groups + dates + groupBy + conditions (full) 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder() 
   .groups(groups) 
   .dates(List.of("12-04-2026", "13-04-2026")) 
   .searchKey("YSA_HEADCODE") 
   .groupBy("DATE", "BRANCH_CODE") 
   .addCondition( 
       new ConditionDto("BRANCH_CODE", "IN", List.of("BR001","BR002")), 
       new ConditionDto("REGION", "=", List.of("WEST")) 
   ) 
   .build(); 

SELECT 
   "DATE", 
   "BRANCH_CODE", 
   CASE 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01036']) THEN 'CASA' 
       WHEN ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) THEN 'Demand Deposit' 
   END AS "GROUP_NAME", 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 
WHERE "DATE" IN ('12-04-2026','13-04-2026') 
 AND ( 
   ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01036']) 
   OR ARRAY_OVERLAP("YSA_HEADCODE", ARRAY['01042','01043']) 
 ) 
 AND ( 
   "BRANCH_CODE" IN ('BR001','BR002') 
   AND "REGION" = ('WEST') 
 ) 
GROUP BY 1, 2, 3 
ORDER BY 1, 2, 3 

What appeared: everything — 2 groupBy columns, date IN, ARRAY_OVERLAP, 2 extra conditions, GROUP BY 1,2,3 

 

Case 6: Dates + conditions only (no groups) 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder() 
   .dates(List.of("21-09-2026")) 
   .addCondition( 
       new ConditionDto("BRANCH_CODE", "IN", List.of("BR001")) 
   ) 
   .build(); 

SELECT 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 
WHERE "DATE" = '21-09-2026' 
 AND ( 
   "BRANCH_CODE" IN ('BR001') 
 ) 

No CASE, no ARRAY_OVERLAP, no GROUP BY. Just a filtered total. 

 

Case 7: groupBy without groups 

new ProductWiseQueryBuilder() 
   .dates(List.of("12-04-2026", "13-04-2026")) 
   .groupBy("DATE") 
   .build(); 

SELECT 
   "DATE", 
   SUM("BALANCE") AS "TOTAL_BALANCE" 
FROM "PRODUCT_WISE" 
WHERE "DATE" IN ('12-04-2026','13-04-2026') 
GROUP BY 1 
ORDER BY 1 

Total balance per date, no head code grouping. 

 

Quick Reference — What Controls What 

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ 
│  .groups(...)     →  CASE in SELECT                            │ 
│                     ARRAY_OVERLAP in WHERE (OR-joined)         │ 
│                     +1 to GROUP BY count                       │ 
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ 
│  .dates(...)      →  WHERE "DATE" = / IN                       │ 
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ 
│  .searchKey(...)  →  column name inside ARRAY_OVERLAP          │ 
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ 
│  .groupBy(...)    →  columns in SELECT                         │ 
│                     increments GROUP BY / ORDER BY ordinals    │ 
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ 
│  .addCondition()  →  AND (col OP (vals)) in WHERE              │ 
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ 

Rule of thumb: call what you need, skip what you don't. The SQL always matches exactly what you asked for. 

 

